/* quoted (cell): LINECALLPARAMFLAGS_ONESTEPTRANSFER = 0x00000080 This bit is used only in conjunction with lineSetupTransfer. It combines the operation of lineSetupTransfer followed by lineDial on the consultation call into a single step. The address to be dialed is specified in the TargetAddress member in LINECALLPARAMS. The original call is placed in onholdpendingtransfer state, just as if lineSetupTransfer were called normally, and the consultation call is established normally. The application must still call lineCompleteTransfer to effect the transfer. This feature is often used when invoking a transfer from a server over a third-party call control link, because such links frequently do not support the normal two-step process. TAPI version 2.0 and later.  [+3 more row(s)] */
